    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Not all protein is created equal. Animal proteins have different impacts on our kidneys, for example, than proteins from plants. Within hours of consuming meat, our kidneys rev up into hyperfiltration mode, dramatically increasing their workload. This is true of a variety of animal proteins. Beef, chicken, and fish all appear to have similar effects. But, an equivalent amount of plant protein causes virtually no noticeable stress on our kidneys. Check out the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/protein/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for a summary and to watch videos like </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-vegetarians-get-enough-protein/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Do Vegetarians Get Enough Protein?</span></a> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">and</span> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-protein-combining-myth/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Protein-Combining Myth</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Recipe: Red Beans and Quinoa</h4>\n<p>\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/red-beans-and-quinoa/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-80475 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-1536x1536.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-2048x2048.jpg 2048w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/red-beans-and-quinoa-3-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>This simple meal comes together quickly and is full of beans, herbs, and spices. Personalize it by swapping out the quinoa for another favorite grain. Check out the recipe on our newly redesigned </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/red-beans-and-quinoa/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">recipe page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CWMdaxtJ0zT/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for a video on how it’s made.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4>The Many Ways to Give</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-84920 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/donate-yt-end-card.png 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>As you know, there are no ads or corporate sponsors on NutritionFacts.org. Our supporters and volunteers are truly the lifeblood of this organization. You enable us to do this work. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">By becoming a monthly donor, you help ensure a predictable and steady stream of support for our nonprofit, and we are very thankful. And, there are even more ways to support us!⁠</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">✅  </span><a href=\"https://smile.amazon.com/gp/chpf/homepage/ref=smi_chpf_redirect?ie=UTF8&amp;ein=05-0559626&amp;ref_=smi_ext_ch_05-0559626_cl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Amazon Smile</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Select NutritionFacts.org as your charity to support using the Smile browser when shopping on Amazon.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">✅ </span><a href=\"https://www.goodshop.com/nonprofit/nutritionfactsorg%E2%81%A0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">GoodShop</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Earn cashback or donate when shopping at more than 7,000 different merchants⁠.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">✅ </span><a href=\"https://givingassistant.org/np#nutritionfacts-org-inc%E2%81%A0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Giving Assistant</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Download the browser extension, and give a percentage of the savings you earn when shopping online to NutritionFacts⁠. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">✅ </span><a href=\"https://symb.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">SYMB</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Round up your spending when you shop using the Symb App, and donate the rounded amounts to NutritionFacts when you select us as your nonprofit of choice.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">✅ </span><a href=\"https://careasy.org/nonprofit/nutritionfacts-org-inc%E2%81%A0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CARS</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Donate your vehicle, and gift the proceeds to NutritionFacts. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">⁠</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Please join us in supporting the evidence-based nutrition revolution by making a tax-deductible donation to NutritionFacts.org today at </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. We also invite you to please consider supporting us in even more ways. See how at </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/giving/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/giving/</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.⁠ Thank you for your support!⁠</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Language Search on NutritionFacts.org</h4>\n<p>\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-80477\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/screenshot-120x90.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/screenshot-120x90.png 120w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/screenshot-500x375.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>Want to see all of the NutritionFacts videos available in your language? Visit our </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/?s=/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">search page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and check out the Subtitle Language menu on the right side of the page. (Press the Filters button if you’re on a mobile.) Select your language, and the results will show all of the videos subtitled in that language.</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/translators/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Consider volunteering</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to help make more videos available in your language!</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Volunteer Spotlight: Liz Gildred</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-80467\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/Liz_2022.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"/>“I started as a Graphic Design Volunteer in October 2021, and it’s been a great experience so far! It has given me a way to make a small contribution to the extremely worthy cause of evidence-based nutrition. I’m happy to have the opportunity to support a much-needed and trustworthy source of information.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One favorite WFPB recipe is my breakfast smoothie. The ingredients have evolved (and snowballed!) over the years. I blend either kale or spinach with avocado, banana, walnuts, flaxseed, chia seed, green tea leaves, lemon zest, cinnamon, turmeric, a pinch of pepper, ginger, amla powder, and chlorella powder, along with any type of plant-based milk and ice cubes.”</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-60211 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-increase-your-life-expectancy-12-to-14-years/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71432\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Large collection of the healthy foods including spinach, garbanzo beans, carrots, beets, ginger.\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-26-How-to-Increase-Your-Life-Expectancy-12-to-14-Years.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-increase-your-life-expectancy-12-to-14-years/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Increase Your Life Expectancy 12 to 14 Years</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What can physicians do to promote healthy, life-extending, lifestyle changes?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-healthiest-type-of-potato/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71416\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Group of homegrown red and purple potatoes in rustic setting with dirt\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-24-The-Healthiest-Type-of-Potato.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-healthiest-type-of-potato/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Healthiest Type of Potato</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Are yellow-fleshed potatoes healthier than white? And, what about the glycoalkaloid toxins?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\n<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-carcinogen-glycidol-in-cooking-oils/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70747\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Cooking oil poured from a bottle into a steel pot\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-18-The-Carcinogen-Glycidol-in-Cooking-Oils.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-carcinogen-glycidol-in-cooking-oils/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Carcinogen Glycidol in Cooking Oils</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Glycidol may help explain why people who eat fried foods get more cancer.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
